```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "fault_kind": "application_method_slow",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind IN ('Server','Internal') GROUP BY span_name, attr_span_kind ORDER BY span_name",
          "claim": "Route-plan getCheapestRoutes and getQuickestRoutes average about 1.86 s in abnormal, while getMinStopStations stays around 20 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "WITH s AS (SELECT trace_id FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND span_name LIKE '%cheapestRoute' AND duration>1e9 LIMIT 1) SELECT t.service_name, t.span_name, t.attr_span_kind, round(t.duration/1e6,1) ms FROM abnormal_traces t JOIN s USING(trace_id) ORDER BY t.time",
          "claim": "In a slow cheapestRoute trace, the 1.86 s sits inside the method span; its only child call takes about 20 ms."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, metric, round(avg(value),3) avgv FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='ts-route-plan-service' AND metric IN ('container.cpu.usage','k8s.pod.cpu.usage','container.memory.usage','k8s.container.restarts') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Route-plan CPU and memory show no saturation during the incident; CPU is lower than normal, so the slowness is in-process."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-route-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-travel-plan-service' AND attr_span_kind IN ('Server','Client') AND (span_name LIKE '%cheapest' OR span_name LIKE '%quickest' OR span_name='POST') GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Travel-plan cheapest and quickest server spans and their outgoing POST calls rise to about 1.06–1.86 s, matching route-plan's slowdown."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-travel-plan-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, count(*) n, round(avg(duration)/1e6,1) avg_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='ts-ui-dashboard' AND attr_span_kind='Server' AND span_name LIKE '%travelPlan%' GROUP BY ALL",
          "claim": "Dashboard's travelPlan cheapest and quickest endpoints average about 1.86 s, while minStation stays around 25 ms."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

The degradation is confined to the travel-plan search endpoints that users reach through `ts-ui-dashboard`. The cheapest and quickest travel-plan requests take about 1.86 s instead of about 50 ms. The minStation variant is unaffected, and no service shows HTTP errors.

The root cause is in `ts-route-plan-service`. Its `getCheapestRoutes` and `getQuickestRoutes` methods spend about 1.85 s in their own code, while the one outgoing call in those spans takes about 20 ms. Its `getMinStopStations` method is normal. CPU and memory show no saturation, and the pod had no restarts, so I classed this as `application_method_slow` rather than a resource fault.

The effect travels up the call chain: `ts-travel-plan-service` waits on route-plan and inherits the latency, and `ts-ui-dashboard` surfaces it to users.

I did not find a second fault. Several services show fewer spans in the abnormal period, but this tracks the lower overall request volume and the changed endpoint mix rather than a separate failure. I have not fully ruled out that the lower volume hides something.
